What does this program print? Use the term **fall-through** in your answer.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void)
{
    int n = 1;
    switch (n) {
        case 1: printf("one ");
        case 2: printf("two "); break;
        default: printf("many ");
    }
    printf("\n");
    return 0;
}
```

