What does this program print? Note that the length `n` is passed separately.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
void double_all(int v[], int n)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        v[i] = v[i] * 2;
}
int main(void)
{
    int a[3] = {1, 2, 3};
    double_all(a, 3);
    printf("%d %d %d\n", a[0], a[1], a[2]);
    return 0;
}
```

